    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-metta-ni-nai-2",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Circumfix built on a pre-predicate adverb. The record's core rule is めったに + verb in the negative (めったに食べない) and it states the predicate is ALWAYS negative, so the pattern's meaning-bearing element sits BEFORE the base and the closed op set has append but no prepend. Steps covering only the negative half would emit 食べない, which is plain negation, not this point. The record's alternative frame ことはめったにない (雪が降ることはめったにない) is suffixal and would be expressible, but it is a nominalized side frame; emitting it alone would present the rarer construction as if it were the rule the record actually teaches.",
      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
