    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-moshikasuru-to-kamoshirenai",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Circumfix around a clause: the record's formation is もしかすると at the START of the sentence plus かもしれない at the END, and its nuance field calls the pair a sandwich that surrounds the clause on both sides. The closed op set only transforms a base and suffixes material to it, so もしかすると cannot be placed in front; steps carrying only the かもしれない tail would emit ordinary かもしれない, which carries none of this point's own material.",
      "nuance_tags": ["conjecture", "softening"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-moshimo-nara",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Pre-posed adverb plus a tail that is a different grammar point. The record's formation is もしも + clause + なら, and everything it specifies about attachment (plain form for verbs and い-adjectives including the past 降ったなら, bare stem for な-adjectives and nouns: 静かなら, 学生なら) belongs to plain なら. Unlike the sibling もし records, this one never states that もしも may be dropped, so emitting the tail alone would both need a prepend op the enum lacks and label the generic なら conditional as this point.",
      "nuance_tags": ["condition", "emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
